ne  a sign said he said Tom Clark there with  the latest from Whitehaven in Cumbria  and hopefully we'll be able to let you  know the government's decision in  tomorrow's show so do join us for that I  mean while the G7 has made uh 15 billion  dollar offer to Vietnam in order to  speed up his transition away from coal  Vietnam which is among the world's top  20 coal users had been due to sign up  for the so-called Just Energy transition  partnership with G7 Nations at the  global cop 27 climate Summits last month  but talks broke off before the meeting  a report by the climate change committee  has warned that what it calls Scotland's  trend of failure in meeting targets to  reduce greenhouse gas emissions will  continue without urgent and strong  action  in its latest reports to discussions  Parliament the CCC noted that Scotland  had missed seven of 11 targets to date  the country's Net Zero secretary Michael  Madison said that the government was  actively considering the ccc's advice  alongside work already started to  prepare a new climate change plan  covering the period to 2040.  person and the U.S have struck a deal to  ensure liquefied natural gas which is  mostly obtained through fracking keeps  flowing into the UK next year well that  agreement will ensure at least nine to  ten billion cubic meters of American LNG  is delivered to the UK over the next  year well that's more than double the  amount exported back in 2021 in the  government's effort to underpin energy  supplies threatened by Russia's war in  Ukraine energy bodies have criticized  The increased Reliance on LNG though  with its higher carbon footprint and  costs alongside the growing Reliance on  overseas vendors compared to  domestically produced gas  LNG is around four times as carbon  intensive as UK Shale making it  considerably less appealing than  domestic supplies  now the U.N Secretary General says that  Humanity has become a weapon of mass  extinction and called in governments to  end 