ause the loss of Nature and  biodiversity comes with a steep human  cost  a cost we measure in lost jobs anger  diseases and deaths Britain is one of  the most nature depleted countries on  the planet  uncertainty of the government's  commitment to environmental regulations  hasn't built confidence that ministers  care but one Insider a former green  campaigner insists things are changing  there are lots of really good things  happening lots of policies still to come  through this is now the moment when we  have to start getting serious it's all  very well to have these targets and have  the policies if they don't make a  difference on the ground then there's  every good reason to ask questions this  Summit will determine the health of  nature for centuries to come but  conservationists warn time is running  out right now the planet is experiencing  the largest loss of life since the  dinosaurs  Thomas More Sky News in gloucestershire  and we'll be keeping you right up to  date with what's happening at cop15  throughout this week and next and also  on tomorrow's show we're hoping to speak  to a delegate live in Montreal well that  is it from us but just a reminder that  you can watch Tom heaps climate show  that will be on Saturdays and Sundays at  3 30 in the afternoon or at 7 30 in the  evening and of course if you have any  questions about the climate change that  you once answered very simple just send  all of your questions through to us  using that QR code which is on your  screen right now we will try to answer  as many as we can on Tom's show  and that is it from me for now thank you  for watching have a lovely day bye for  now

